1
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:35,100
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:40,100
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:44,100
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:49,100
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:52,100
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:55,100
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:58,100
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:01,100
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,100
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:07,100
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:11,100
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:15,100
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:22,100
Unable to save Ace's life during the War of the Best,

14
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:27,100
the injured Luffy was taken to Amazon Livy, where he fell into despair.

15
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:30,100
But this is a story from ten years ago.

16
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:35,100
Ace, Sabo, and Luffy prepare for battle with a giant tiger

17
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:39,100
to decide which of the three is best suited to be a pirate captain.

18
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:43,100
While out hunting, they meet a former captain named Naguri,

19
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,100
who once challenged Gold Roger.

20
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:49,100
At Luffy's request, he agrees to share some of his wisdom.

21
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:58,100
The battle against the big tiger! Who's going to be captain?

22
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,100
Unable to escape a map.

23
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:11,380
torso falls both theouncer's

24
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,080
21 creature, but palabraא� color

25
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,100
I assaulted you and Mike.

26
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:18,100
How did you think that was a good plan,

27
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:23,100
we could have snuck around behind it or I don't know anything?

28
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:28,100
Yeah, cause your idea worked out great!

29
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,100
Okay, not our finest hour.

30
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:53,100
Let's put some poison mushrooms in the bait tomorrow.

31
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,100
That should slow him down.

32
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,100
Hold on a sec.

33
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,100
That tiger may be big, but at the end of the day,

34
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,100
he's still a cat, right?

35
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:04,100
So what do you say we give Catnib a try?

36
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,100
Hello?

37
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:13,100
I wonder how Luffy's doing with his secret training.

38
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,100
I don't know if you noticed,

39
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,100
but it's been a whole week since he left.

40
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:20,100
We should probably pay him a visit, don't you think?

41
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,100
You know how he can be.

42
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:25,100
Maybe the training is too hard on him,

43
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,100
and he's like,

44
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:28,100
No! I just want to go home!

45
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,100
Wait!

46
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:32,100
What if we haven't heard anything from him

47
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,100
cause he's dead already!

48
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,100
Luffy!

49
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,100
What, Sabo?

50
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,100
Oh, come on!

51
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:51,100
Don't you care about your little brother at all?

52
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,100
Stop playing cool!

53
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,100
Shut up!

54
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:55,100
He's the one who left.

55
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:57,100
It's not my problem if he dies.

56
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:58,100
Listen!

57
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:01,100
I don't know who you're trying to impress with this,

58
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,100
but Luffy!

59
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:05,100
What the hell?

60
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:16,100
Oh, oops!

61
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,100
Sorry, you okay?

62
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,100
Luffy!

63
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,100
Hey, Sabo!

64
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,100
Hey, what's up, guys?

65
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:30,100
How have you been?

66
00:06:30,100 --> 00:06:33,100
I'm pretty good.

67
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,100
What's that?

68
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,100
A target?

69
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,100
Oh, you noticed, huh?

70
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:49,100
Now, let me show you the moves I've been working on.

71
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,100
Here we go!

72
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:53,100
Gum gum!

73
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:56,100
Pistol!

74
00:06:56,100 --> 00:07:09,100
Uh-oh!

75
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:12,100
Not bad at all.

76
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:15,100
Your aim still sucks, but your reach has gotten pretty far.

77
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:17,100
I meant to do that!

78
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,100
Not this again!

79
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,100
What kind of special training have you been giving him?

80
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:24,100
None, really.

81
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:28,100
To be honest, I've just been having him chop some wood every day.

82
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:31,100
All the work might have helped him build a bit of muscle,

83
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:33,100
but I can hardly take credit for that.

84
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:42,100
My men, at the height of our strength, challenged Roger to a fight.

85
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,100
Really?

86
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,100
A fight that we lost.

87
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:48,100
Put in our place, we all split up.

88
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:55,100
You hate him too, don't you?

89
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:57,100
I don't follow.

90
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:00,100
Because he defeated your old crew.

91
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,100
Oh, you mean Roger. I see.

92
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:07,100
I was rather devastated, that much is true.

93
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:11,100
But the only reason I lost to Roger was because I wasn't strong enough.

94
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:15,100
In that respect, he taught me a valuable lesson.

95
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,100
What, by kicking your ass?

96
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:19,100
In a way, yes.

97
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,100
We surrender.

98
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,100
We never stood a chance.

99
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:31,100
Cut off my head, I don't care.

100
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:35,100
But please, please, spare my crew in return.

101
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:38,100
I take responsibility for our foolishness.

102
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:41,100
Captain, no!

103
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,100
I beg of you.

104
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,100
Huh?

105
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:56,100
Cold Roger was a man of extraordinary character indeed.

106
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,100
And that's why I say he...

107
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,100
Stop lying!

108
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:02,100
If he's so great, then why does everybody hate him, huh?

109
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:08,100
Did those men fight with Roger?

110
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:11,100
Did they even meet him face to face?

111
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:12,100
Huh?

112
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:15,100
In the world of pirates, if you lose a fight, you lose your life.

113
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:18,100
And yet Roger chose to spare mine.

114
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:22,100
So, if those pirates did face him, they should be grateful.

115
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:25,100
Complaining like that is a luxury, you know.

116
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:28,100
One they only have because their lives were spared.

117
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,100
You watch, I'll get even stronger.

118
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:34,100
If Roger had a son, you think he should be grateful too?

119
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:41,100
Actually, I'd feel sorry for him.

120
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:46,100
Regardless of his path, his father's name would haunt him wherever he went.

121
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:50,100
With a legacy like that, I wouldn't blame him for resenting the man.

122
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:53,100
And it's not like he could talk it out with him either.

123
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:57,100
At any rate, if I were his son, I wouldn't want to be a pirate.

124
00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:03,100
His name could scarcely do me any favors, and more likely than not, it would put a target on my back.

125
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:05,100
What the hell do you know, huh?

126
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:07,100
I'm sick of hearing your crappy lectures.

127
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,100
You really think you're some great pirate?

128
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:12,100
Prove it! Fight me!

129
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:15,100
Whoa, what?

130
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:18,100
I'd be careful, boy.

131
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:21,100
Like I said, you lose a fight, you lose your life.

132
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,100
I'm never going to lose to you!

133
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,100
You've still got some growing to do.

134
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:47,100
Damn it! Spare me another lecture and just finish me off!

135
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:51,100
I'll spare you the lecture and a violent death if you'll come with me.

136
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,100
Huh?

137
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,100
You're gonna love this!

138
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:04,100
Oh, wow! I didn't know there was a cove down here.

139
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,100
This place is pretty cool.

140
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:10,100
Come on! Stop gawking and hurry up!

141
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:13,100
Go! Go!

142
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,100
Let's see some hustle!

143
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,100
Okay, geez, what's the big deal?

144
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:21,100
Why don't you look and see?

145
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:25,100
Holy crap!

146
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:28,100
It's huge!

147
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,100
Not bad, huh?

148
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:34,100
A real-life secret pirate ship!

149
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,100
Wait, that's crazy!

150
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:39,100
This is why you collected all those parts?

151
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:42,100
Since I've been working all alone, it's gone a bit slow.

152
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,100
Anyhow, you boys are pretty tough.

153
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,100
Do you think you could lend me a hand?

154
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,100
Huh?

155
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,100
Why would I do that?

156
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:52,100
Because I spared your life, you ungrateful little snot.

157
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:57,100
That's fine for Ace, but how did I get looped into this mess?

158
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:59,100
Well, you did follow us.

159
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:01,100
What is this, a child labor scheme?

160
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:05,100
I'm too busy hunting that tiger to waste time on some ship.

161
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:08,100
I can give you some tiger hunting pointers if you stick around.

162
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,100
Yeah?

163
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,100
Okay, maybe.

164
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,100
I got one question.

165
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:17,100
What are you gonna do when the ship is done?

166
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,100
Huh.

167
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,100
I'm taking it to sea, of course.

168
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:25,100
To find my crewmates that split up all those years ago.

169
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,100
You sure you're up to that?

170
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:28,100
And why not?

171
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,100
I was a captain once.

172
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:30,100
I'm hardly some rookie.

173
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,100
I know.

174
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,100
That's kinda what I'm saying.

175
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:37,100
No matter how old you are, you can always chase your dream.

176
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:41,100
I'm sailing again and nobody can stop me.

177
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,100
Once a pirate, always a pirate.

178
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,100
You kids got a problem with that?

179
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,100
Nuh-uh!

180
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:50,100
Well, I'm not gonna stop you.

181
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,100
Ace?

182
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:54,100
You spared my life.

183
00:12:54,100 --> 00:12:55,100
What can I say?

184
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,100
I'll help you build your ship.

185
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,100
For now.

186
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,100
Cause I'm beating you tomorrow.

187
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,100
That's Ace for you.

188
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:18,100
And thus began their training with Nagari, building his ship, day in and day out.

189
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:21,100
With every heavy log they lifted, they grew stronger.

190
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:24,100
And with every sparring match, they honed their skills.

191
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:30,100
Although the work was intense, bit by bit, they learned what it truly meant to be a pirate.

192
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:39,100
Spring always seems to arrive late in Grey Terminal, but even the most stubborn of snow eventually gives way to warm weather.

193
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,100
Warm weather.

194
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:50,100
I'm not losing!

195
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:52,100
Neither am I!

196
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,100
I'm beating both of you!

197
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,100
Get ready!

198
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,100
Now come, come!

199
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,100
Pistol!

200
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:09,100
Every damn time! What is wrong with you?

201
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,100
Sorry!

202
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,100
Listen boys, you've done this enough already.

203
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:18,100
There's more to being a pirate than just whacking everyone with a pipe.

204
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,100
Surely you want more than strength.

205
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:23,100
Yeah, all that stuff can wait.

206
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:27,100
Right now we want to be strong cause the strongest one of us gets to be the captain.

207
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,100
Why do you think we're training, huh?

208
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,100
Remember?

209
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:32,100
Whoever beats the tiger wins!

210
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,100
The tiger again.

211
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:38,100
I agree that a captain needs to be tough, but there's something more important than that, you see?

212
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:42,100
A different kind of strength that can triumph over any foe.

213
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,100
Can you teach us that?

214
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:47,100
Oh, curious, are you?

215
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,100
It slips my mind.

216
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,100
There's no secret!

217
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,100
You're making stuff up!

218
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:01,100
No, I really forgot.

219
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,100
Shh, shh, shh.

220
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:28,100
Can't sleep?

221
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,100
I'm sorry if my hammering's too loud.

222
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,100
Hmm.

223
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,100
What, is something the matter?

224
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:38,100
What does it take to be a captain?

225
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:42,100
If there really is a way for me to be stronger, I have to know what it is!

226
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:43,100
So just tell me!

227
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:44,100
Alright then.

228
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,100
I'll be honest.

229
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:48,100
Even after all these years, I'm not sure.

230
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,100
Fine.

231
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:52,100
Why do you think we're a captain?

232
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:54,100
I'm sorry if my hammering's too loud.

233
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:56,100
Hmm, what.

234
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:57,100
Is something the matter?

235
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:58,280
I have to know what it is.

236
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,520
So just tell me.

237
00:16:02,300 --> 00:16:03,400
All right, then.

238
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:06,760
I'll be honest.

239
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:11,540
Even after all these years, I'm not sure.

240
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,420
Frankly, I don't think I was a very good captain.

241
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:19,480
But my crew, they still followed me.

242
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:24,480
Right to the end, they called me captain without any doubt.

243
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:29,060
And so, in a way, I'm still captain of the Nagori Pirates.

244
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:33,180
Not because of my strength, but because of the approval of my crew.

245
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,540
That's the true test of a captain.

246
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:37,740
Or so I always say.

247
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:41,800
Ha. Bunch of crap.

248
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:42,680
Huh?

249
00:16:54,480 --> 00:17:00,560
Alright! We did it!

250
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:03,640
Okay. Not bad. I'm jealous.

251
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,880
Awesome! Too cool!

252
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,720
I couldn't have done it without all your help.

253
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:09,980
Thank you, boys.

254
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,260
I really mean that.

255
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:16,240
So is this it?

256
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:18,140
Like, are you leaving now?

257
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:18,840
Not yet.

258
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,760
I have one last loose end.

259
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:24,320
I think it's about time we finish that training of yours, eh?

260
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:28,240
So, are you boys ready to go tiger hunting or what?

261
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,440
Wait, for real?

262
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:34,000
I'm gonna kill him and put this crappy training behind me for good.

263
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,180
Yeah, except I'm gonna kill him.

264
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:37,920
I'm gonna double kill him!

265
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:50,720
Here it comes.

266
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,780
He certainly hasn't gotten any smaller.

267
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:05,980
I got this!

268
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:14,140
I'm a lot faster now!

269
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,340
And stronger.

270
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:31,980
Over here!

271
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,480
You gotta pay attention, big guy!

272
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:37,200
Just give up already!

273
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:47,420
Are you okay?

274
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:48,960
Hey, Ace!

275
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:58,240
Come on!

276
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,540
Now go, go!

277
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,440
And hit the ball!

278
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:11,300
Ah, crap!

279
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:12,220
Luffy!

280
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,440
Run away!

281
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:28,600
You saved me!

282
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:29,600
So heavy.

283
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,680
I thought we were strong.

284
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,060
No.

285
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,880
There's still one thing none of us have.

286
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:42,320
Not because of my strength, because of the approval of my crew.

287
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,420
We've come too far to give up now.

288
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:47,920
All right, you guys.

289
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:49,040
Teamwork!

290
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:49,480
What?

291
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:49,540
What?

292
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:49,600
What?

293
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:50,000
What?

294
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:50,680
Ah.

295
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:53,740
Seems things are finally getting interesting.

296
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,140
We're not fast enough on our own.

297
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:02,240
But with Luffy's powers, maybe we can make something happen.

298
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:04,220
Sabo, keep it busy!

299
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:05,680
I'm on it!

300
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:07,840
He's stupid over here!

301
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:09,200
Eat me, not them, okay?

302
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,280
Now kiss my ass!

303
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:12,580
Ah!

304
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,260
Okay, you ready?

305
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:17,020
Yeah!

306
00:20:18,740 --> 00:20:20,640
Pull back as far as you can and wait!

307
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:22,660
Sabo, this way!

308
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:26,040
I hope this works, because I think I'm about to die!

309
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,360
You're going to be okay!

310
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,660
Just a little bit more and he's history!

311
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:35,220
Ah!

312
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:37,480
You know what we're doing next, right?

313
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,280
Huh?

314
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:42,020
Ah!

315
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,020
Um, um!

316
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,540
Rocket!

317
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,040
Ah!

318
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,040
Ah!

319
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,220
All right!

320
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:12,480
Wait, we just helped Ace be the captain.

321
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:16,980
We worked for like a million years on this.

322
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,220
That's the deal. We all agreed.

323
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:22,500
Damn it. Stop your complaining.

324
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,240
I'm not going to be the stupid captain, okay?

325
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:27,720
Huh? Why not?

326
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,100
I don't know. It doesn't feel right.

327
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:32,580
You two kicked as much ass as I did.

328
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,260
Fair enough.

329
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:35,720
Well, for now.

330
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:38,520
But one of these days, I'm going to kick so much ass,

331
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:39,600
it'll blow your mind,

332
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:42,040
and you're both going to be begging to join my crew.

333
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:44,940
Are you going to beg over my dead body?

334
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:47,020
What? Just you wait.

335
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:51,460
I couldn't have asked for a better ending.

336
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,660
My work here is done.

337
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:55,640
So long, boys.

338
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:56,920
Nogity!

339
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:58,160
Hmm?

340
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:00,760
I know you're old, but you can't die yet.

341
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:03,880
I still want a rematch. I never did get to beat you.

342
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:06,740
See ya!

343
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:09,120
Bon voyage and good luck!

344
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:10,220
Huh.

345
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:12,800
I have a feeling we'll meet again.

346
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:13,660
Soon.

347
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:34,520
Thus, they bid farewell to their teacher, Nagari.

348
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:38,100
A little stronger and a little wiser,

349
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:41,440
they continued on their path to be pirates.

350
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:49,580
I trust you know where we can find the boy.

351
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:51,420
Yes, sir.

352
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,940
I've kept a close eye on him.

353
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:56,160
I think we've waited long enough.

354
00:22:57,640 --> 00:23:00,160
Why don't you call him and share the good news?

355
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:03,560
Let him know that Sabo's coming home.

356
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:12,660
Sabo's days of adventure come to an end

357
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:16,180
as he is forced to remain in Hightown apart from his friends.

358
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:19,140
However, fate soon brings the three boys together again

359
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:22,040
as Luffy and Ace take on work for the pirate Blue Jam

360
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:25,240
and Sabo uncovers a terrifying conspiracy.

361
00:23:25,620 --> 00:23:27,000
On the next, One Piece.

362
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:28,720
Freedom taken away.

363
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:31,260
The nobles' plot closing in on the brothers.

364
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,480
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

